  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit. The most informative first experiment is to establish a minimal baseline: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 (config_001). This configuration has the fewest design decisions (no aggregation, no fusion, no image encoder), making it a clean reference point. It tests the fundamental question: how well does a simple PCA-reduced RNA representation perform on this task? From this baseline, subsequent experiments can isolate the marginal contribution of each added complexity—multiprofile/aggregation (config_002/003), alternative RNA encoders (config_004/007), image modality (config_010), and multimodal fusion (config_016/017). Starting with the simplest configuration avoids conflating multiple design choices and ensures that any later performance gains can be attributed to specific additions rather than to an unknown interaction of several untested components simultaneously."
}

